# =============================================================================
# Build-context exclusions.
#
# 🔴 WHY THIS FILE IS NOT COSMETIC. The builder stage does:
#
#     COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules
#     COPY . .
#
# `COPY . .` runs SECOND, so without this file a developer's local
# `node_modules` is overlaid on top of the one `npm ci` just built inside
# Alpine. The result is a MERGED tree — a verification build made on Windows
# produced an image containing BOTH `@img/sharp-win32-x64` and
# `@img/sharp-linuxmusl-x64`. The platform binaries that `npm ci` resolved are
# silently mixed with foreign ones, and the image stops being a function of the
# lockfile.
#
# Railway builds from the git repository, where none of these paths exist, so
# this file is what makes a LOCAL build reproduce the Railway build rather than
# quietly diverging from it.
#
# ⚠️ `.env.ci*` must NOT be excluded — the Dockerfile copies it as the
# build-time dummy environment (see Dockerfile, BUILD_ENV_FILE).
# =============================================================================

# --- Dependencies and build output: rebuilt inside the image ----------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Real environment files: NEVER into a build layer -----------------------
# `.env.example`, `.env.ci.example` and `.env.test` are dummy-only and stay.
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.ci

# --- VCS / editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Local runtime artefacts ------------------------------------------------
media/
documents/
.tmp/
coverage/
.vitest/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- Not needed to build or run ---------------------------------------------
docs/
docker-compose*.yml
